{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792399354,"nonce":"GLsQSQc7Fi9goODP1+/CGS29Kgw=","title":"The media Player stops following the native player when playing starts after play() returns, so its animations stop with the audio playing","message":"**What happens**\n\nPress play, or resume after a pause, and the audio plays but everything the app draws from the Player stays as it was: the visualizer and equalizer, the elapsed time, the progress bar. In the dashboard it showed as \"the music player animations no longer play\", with the music still audible.\n\n**Cause**\n\nPlayer.play() calls native.play(), then refresh() and wake(). A browser's native player (xavi's page agent) answers asynchronously, so refresh() reads the state Paused. wake()'s ticker stops as soon as the state is not Seeking, Opening, Playing or Buffering: it ran once, saw Paused and ended. When the audio then started, nothing was polling, so state and position never updated. It is a race, so it came and went with how fast the agent answered (a server that offers byte ranges starts the element at once).\n\n**Fix**\n\nThe ticker also keeps going while playing is intended (playIntent) and the state is not Ended, Failed, Closed or Empty. wake() now asks the scheduler's Ticker whether it still runs, instead of keeping a flag the ticker clears itself.\n\n**Reproducer**\n\ntests/wasm/dashboard_check.mjs: pause, press play again, and the visualizer region must move. It fails on the build before the fix.","files":null}]}